## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: 3 câu hỏi phỏng vấn

**Q1. "Walk me through what happens when you deploy."**
> *"I push to main. GitHub triggers Render, which runs npm ci and a TypeScript build, then starts the new instance and waits for the health check to pass before routing traffic to it. The old instance gets a SIGTERM, and I handle that — I stop accepting new requests and let in-flight ones finish before exiting. Without that, every deploy cuts off a few requests mid-flight."*

**Q2. "Your API is slow on the first call. Why?"**
> *"That's a cold start. I'm on a free tier that spins the service down after fifteen minutes of no traffic, so the first request pays for the container starting up — thirty to sixty seconds.*
> *I decided not to hide it. The client has a longer timeout on the first call after launch and shows a message saying the server is waking up. People tolerate waiting when they know what they're waiting for. I also have a scheduled job that pings the health endpoint, but I treat the honest client behavior as the real fix, not the ping."*

**Q3. "How do you debug a problem a user reports?"**
> *"Every request gets a UUID. It goes into every log line for that request, and it comes back to the client in the error response. So the user gives me that ID, I search the logs, and I have the whole request. Before I had that, debugging was guessing based on a timestamp."*

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `in-flight` | đang giữa chừng | *Let in-flight requests finish.* |
| `spin down / spin up` | tắt bớt / khởi động lên | *The free tier spins down after 15 minutes.* |
| `cut off mid-flight` | cắt giữa chừng | *Every deploy cuts requests off mid-flight.* |
| `tolerate` (v) | chịu được | *People tolerate waiting when they know why.* |
| `route traffic` | dẫn lưu lượng | *It waits before routing traffic to the new instance.* |

